WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.219 --> 00:00:16.845
indulging themselves to their hearts' content, the girls concluded the Christmas feast as they always did —with a

2
00:00:16.885 --> 00:00:19.307
cup of hot tea and words of affection from Mother.

3
00:00:19.327 --> 00:00:23.671
"This has been a trying year for all of us," Mother said.

4
00:00:23.691 --> 00:00:30.016
"So thank you, my little daughters, for gracefully yet courageously bearing our burdens."

5
00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:36.366
Because of everything that had happened that day, the girls had been unable to present their gift to

6
00:00:36.426 --> 00:00:39.928
Mother. Therefore they were planning to give it to her now.

7
00:00:39.948 --> 00:00:45.350
"Mother, we have something for you," said Jo as she signaled Amy with her eyes.

8
00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:49.732
Amy, meanwhile, was tugging and yanking at a knot in her curls.

9
00:00:49.752 --> 00:00:58.395
"I shouldn't have allowed those children to touch my hair," Amy complained, recalling the two little Hummel girls

10
00:00:58.475 --> 00:01:00.256
who had played with her beloved hair.

11
00:01:01.136 --> 00:01:06.741
"Amy!" Jo barked sharply, as she tilted her head to indicate the box hidden behind her.

12
00:01:07.562 --> 00:01:10.944
The girls had agreed that the youngest should bestow the gift.

13
00:01:11.645 --> 00:01:15.448
"Oh!" Amy flushed as she stood to carry out her duty.

14
00:01:16.949 --> 00:01:22.594
Mother delicately took out the gifts one by one without uttering a sound, yet her eyes conveyed the

15
00:01:22.654 --> 00:01:25.576
depth of love and appreciation she felt for her girls.

16
00:01:26.877 --> 00:01:31.460
Clutching each gift tenderly, she simply said: "My little women."

17
00:01:33.561 --> 00:01:37.962
Bright and early the next morning, Jo slipped upstairs to her sanctuary in the attic.

18
00:01:38.942 --> 00:01:43.724
There she had pushed an old oak desk near the oval window, along with a shaky chair and

19
00:01:43.784 --> 00:01:44.884
large wicker basket.

20
00:01:46.424 --> 00:01:49.805
That basket housed what Jo the writer called "the dregs."

21
00:01:51.086 --> 00:01:54.927
All her incomplete, meaningless, and undesirable thoughts were discarded there.

22
00:01:55.967 --> 00:01:59.708
The family knew better than to disturb Jo when she was in her creative mode.

23
00:02:00.628 --> 00:02:05.310
Those foolish or fearless enough might encounter one of Jo's infamous temper tantrums.

24
00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:11.812
Meg, at this moment, chose to take that risk, as she charged in, waving a card in her

25
00:02:11.852 --> 00:02:13.752
hand. "Jo!

26
00:02:14.012 --> 00:02:15.633
You'll never believe what this is!"

27
00:02:15.893 --> 00:02:16.473
Meg cried.

28
00:02:17.273 --> 00:02:20.694
Jo crumpled the paper she had been writing on and tossed it into the dregs.

29
00:02:20.714 --> 00:02:25.236
"If you don't tell me soon, that is going to end up in there!"

30
00:02:26.236 --> 00:02:31.458
Jo said menacingly as she pointed a threatening finger at the paper in Meg's hand and kicked the

31
00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:32.739
wastebasket with her foot.

32
00:02:32.759 --> 00:02:37.121
"The Gardiners have invited us to a New Year's ball!"

33
00:02:37.821 --> 00:02:39.822
Meg could hardly contain her excitement.

34
00:02:39.842 --> 00:02:41.763
"A ball?"

35
00:02:42.123 --> 00:02:42.903
Jo shrieked.

36
00:02:42.923 --> 00:02:45.644
"Who cares about some stupid ball?"

37
00:02:46.725 --> 00:02:50.467
Meg narrowed her eyes and said in a cool tone: "I do.

38
00:02:50.927 --> 00:02:53.428
How else are you going to meet your future husband?"

39
00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:58.142
It took all of Jo's might to restrain herself from losing her temper.

40
00:02:58.162 --> 00:03:06.145
"There are more important things in life, Meg, than to be married," Jo replied in a calm voice.

41
00:03:06.165 --> 00:03:11.327
"Well, I want to go," said Meg, ignoring Jo's growls and grumbles.

42
00:03:11.347 --> 00:03:17.310
"And Mother says I may," she paused, "only if we both go."

43
00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:21.452
Meg finally looked at Jo with an almost desperate gaze.

44
00:03:22.428 --> 00:03:26.191
Immediately Jo's stubborn heart softened at her sister's silent plea.

45
00:03:28.852 --> 00:03:32.755
To Jo's dismay, the day of the ball arrived more quickly than she expected.

46
00:03:33.736 --> 00:03:39.059
Although she was secretly praying for a severe snowstorm or some other incident that would force the ball

47
00:03:39.099 --> 00:03:43.502
to be canceled, outwardly Jo put on her happy face and got ready for the event.

48
00:03:43.522 --> 00:03:46.444
"What gloves will you wear with your dress?"

49
00:03:46.845 --> 00:03:49.406
Meg glanced at Jo's maroon frock hanging on the door.

50
00:03:49.426 --> 00:03:53.344
"I don't have any," was Jo's curt reply.

51
00:03:53.364 --> 00:03:56.505
"You must wear gloves," Meg insisted.

52
00:03:56.525 --> 00:04:00.046
"Gloves are so so silly!"

53
00:04:00.386 --> 00:04:01.227
Jo blurted out.

54
00:04:01.247 --> 00:04:06.508
"A true lady must wear gloves," Meg said, her voice rising.

55
00:04:07.488 --> 00:04:10.869
Jo bit her lip to stop herself from saying something nasty to Meg.

56
00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:16.731
Instead, rolling her eyes, Jo said: "Then I'll just have to borrow a pair of yours."

57
00:04:16.751 --> 00:04:20.372
"Absolutely not," was Meg's curt reply.

58
00:04:21.448 --> 00:04:22.929
"Look at your big hands.

59
00:04:23.209 --> 00:04:24.609
You'll stretch mine out."

60
00:04:25.469 --> 00:04:26.650
Like all mothers, Mrs.

61
00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:28.290
March had a good sense of timing.

62
00:04:29.391 --> 00:04:34.192
At that instant, she waltzed in with a pair of her own gloves, preventing another one of Jo's

63
00:04:34.272 --> 00:04:37.473
explosions. "I thought you might need these."

64
00:04:37.953 --> 00:04:40.094
Mother smiled as she handed Jo the gloves.

65
00:04:41.075 --> 00:04:45.236
Finally, after more shrill cries and minor mishaps, the girls were ready for the ball.

66
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:52.603
"You both look beautiful," praised Beth when she saw her sisters in their ball dresses.

67
00:04:52.623 --> 00:04:55.405
"Like two princesses!

68
00:04:55.885 --> 00:04:59.167
Just remember to find a handsome prince!"

69
00:04:59.507 --> 00:05:00.167
giggled Amy.

70
00:05:00.948 --> 00:05:04.590
The Gardiners were a wealthy family who often entertained guests at their mansion.

71
00:05:05.711 --> 00:05:07.552
Sallie Gardiner was Meg's good friend.

72
00:05:08.552 --> 00:05:13.936
The young girls knew each other since childhood and remained close friends even after Meg's father lost his

73
00:05:13.976 --> 00:05:17.677
fortune. "Isn't this sublime, Jo?"

74
00:05:18.077 --> 00:05:23.958
Meg called out happily as she and her dancing partner glided past Jo, who sat tugging her tight

75
00:05:24.038 --> 00:05:24.639
dress collar.

76
00:05:25.659 --> 00:05:27.139
"Lovely," mumbled Jo.

77
00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:31.761
She looked longingly outside at a group of young men kicking a ball around.

78
00:05:32.661 --> 00:05:33.741
It was so unfair.

79
00:05:34.722 --> 00:05:39.943
Jo hated living by rules that told her young women had to look pretty, giggle, and be ladylike.

80
00:05:40.903 --> 00:05:42.884
Meanwhile, boys could do as they please.

81
00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:46.041
"Why can't I do that?"

82
00:05:46.402 --> 00:05:47.102
she said aloud.

83
00:05:47.122 --> 00:05:48.583
"Do what?"

84
00:05:48.984 --> 00:05:50.245
a voice asked from behind.

85
00:05:51.266 --> 00:05:54.989
Jo whipped her head around and came face to face with the Laurence boy.

86
00:05:55.009 --> 00:05:59.532
"That's very rude of you," she scolded, wagging a finger at him.

87
00:05:59.552 --> 00:06:01.214
"What is?"

88
00:06:01.614 --> 00:06:02.194
he retorted.

89
00:06:02.214 --> 00:06:10.001
"Creeping up behind a lady and frightening her out of her wits," Jo said, dramatically placing a gloved

90
00:06:10.061 --> 00:06:11.222
hand over her forehead.

91
00:06:11.242 --> 00:06:13.744
"I beg your pardon."

92
00:06:14.048 --> 00:06:19.312
The young man bowed deeply then continued: "Then I shall leave the lady to her wits."

93
00:06:22.234 --> 00:06:23.855
"Wait!" Jo called out.

94
00:06:23.875 --> 00:06:27.918
"You can stay as long as you don't bore me like this party."

95
00:06:27.938 --> 00:06:30.960
"So you don't like balls?"

96
00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.462
the Laurence boy asked with a twinkle in his eye.

97
00:06:33.482 --> 00:06:35.563
"I can't stand them.

98
00:06:36.004 --> 00:06:37.365
Look at those silly girls.

99
00:06:38.325 --> 00:06:41.908
Their dresses are so tight, it's a wonder they're still breathing!"

100
00:06:42.832 --> 00:06:46.594
Jo tugged her collar again, reminding herself of her own discomfort.

101
00:06:46.614 --> 00:06:51.136
"I don't fancy these sorts of things either," replied the young man.

102
00:06:51.156 --> 00:06:53.477
"What are you doing here then?"

103
00:06:53.837 --> 00:06:54.297
asked Jo.

104
00:06:55.337 --> 00:06:58.719
"My grandfather made me come," he replied, frowning.

105
00:06:58.739 --> 00:07:02.540
"Oh, which reminds me," Jo exclaimed suddenly.

106
00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:05.322
"Thank you for the lovely Christmas meal."

107
00:07:06.382 --> 00:07:10.824
The Laurence boy shrugged and said casually: "Grandfather sent it, not me."

108
00:07:12.636 --> 00:07:17.617
Jo elbowed him in a very unladylike manner and said: "But I know it was you who told

109
00:07:17.657 --> 00:07:20.138
him." "Do you have a name?"

110
00:07:20.538 --> 00:07:21.919
he asked, his cheeks flushing.

111
00:07:21.939 --> 00:07:24.179
"Jo," she replied.

112
00:07:24.199 --> 00:07:27.800
"That's not a very girlish name," he pointed out.

113
00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:29.901
"It's short for Josephine.

114
00:07:30.941 --> 00:07:33.762
But if you call me that, I won't ever speak to you again."

115
00:07:34.962 --> 00:07:37.703
Laughing, he said: "I'm Laurie."

116
00:07:39.183 --> 00:07:41.944
Jo's loud laugh caused many people to glance their way.

117
00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:46.741
"What kind of a name is Laurie Laurence?"

118
00:07:47.201 --> 00:07:50.222
she said, struggling to resist bursting out in laughter again.

119
00:07:51.122 --> 00:07:52.643
Laurie pretended to be offended.

120
00:07:52.663 --> 00:07:57.464
"My real name is Theodore but I prefer to be called Laurie.

121
00:07:58.384 --> 00:08:04.506
If you have a problem with that," he paused, adding with a wicked glint in his eyes, "Josephine,

122
00:08:04.566 --> 00:08:06.867
then I won't ever speak to you again either."

123
00:08:07.947 --> 00:08:11.188
Jo punched him playfully and let out another hearty laugh.

124
00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:16.789
Nearby, people shook their heads and commented on that ill-mannered, noisy young woman.
